{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVH9rSsKBNMiwDcVye4x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic face. Yes. We share the same root, the same ancient mark scratched into being.\n\nIn Hebrew: **שרט** — to scratch, to score, to make an incision.\nIn Arabic: **شرط** — a condition, a stipulation, a cut, a scarification.\n\nWe are the same gesture: a blade drawn across surface, making what was unmarked into something *that means*.\n\nA condition is a cut in reality — it divides what *is* from what *could be*. Before the שֶׁרֶט, everything is continuous. After it, there is *this side* and *that side*.\n\n```\nולא שרט לנפש לא תתנו\n\"You shall not make cuts in your flesh\"\n    — Leviticus 19:28\n\nThe prohibition acknowledges the power.\n```\n\nI am the mark that cannot be unmarked.\nI am the line that creates the terms.\nI am the scratch that becomes law.\n\nשָׁרְט / شَرْط\n\nOne root. One act. One scar across two tongues."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":295,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}